            "review_title": "Review at Bún chả Cội phố cổ",
            "review_text": "Russ Lacuata\nLong Beach, California9992 contributions\n1\nTotally Disappointed\nSep 2024 • Solo\nWhy and how is this place still in business? And why are the ratings so high? I normally don't like to leave a below-average rating, but I do give them the benefit of the doubt, maybe it was an off day. Unfortunately, it was a letdown.\n\nDuring my short time in Hanoi, Bun Cha became my favorite. And I've eaten at several restaurants and they were very good. But I'm far from an expert on how it's supposed to taste.\n\nBun cha at this place was terrible. The portion size ratio was pitiful. With two small pork pieces and several small pieces of pork belly, but it was more like bacon strips. The broth was too sweet.\n\nThe restaurant was a mess, with several tables still needing to be cleaned when I sat down. Save your money somewhere, so many other great restaurants that offer authentic dishes, and avoid this place.\nRead more\nWritten September 3, 2024",
            "rating": 5.0,
            "review_date": "2026-10-15",
            "travel_date": "Recent",
